We need to implement a function block FB that meets all the requirements. The function block has the given inputs and outputs.

Goal: Write a ST program (IEC 61131-3) for FB.

We must obey constraints: Only one code block, no extra text. Use VAR_INPUT, VAR_OUTPUT, etc.

We must ensure mutual exclusion MotorForward and MotorReverse (S1). MotorForward only possible in auto mode or when manual ForwardButton pressed (S2). MotorReverse only in manual and ReverseButton pressed (S3). CompletionLight only when auto and SensorC detection (S4). CompletionLight must turn off next cycle after SensorC no longer detected (S5). Additional properties: in manual mode, exactly one direction button pressed yields motor output accordingly (S7). Mode switch from manual to auto or power-up, and if SensorA and ButtonA, motor forward (S8). Sequence from A->B->C: detection, stop motor, etc (S6). Additional S9-12 guarantee.

We need to implement internal state: need to know previous mode, previous sensor states maybe to detect edge (rising/falling). Also need to track which station product currently at. Possibly a simple state machine: eIdle (no product), atA (product at A, awaiting ButtonA), movingAB (motor forward), atB (product at B, awaiting ButtonB), movingBC (motor forward), atC (product at C, awaiting ButtonC), completed (light on). At power-up or mode change to auto, if SensorA present and ButtonA, we may start moving.

But the formal properties require careful handling of edge detection and latching.

Simplify: We'll treat the product as moving automatically based on sensors and buttons. Since product cannot be partially moved (e.g., motor forward moves product from A to B automatically, stops when SensorB detection). However, product movement is not simulated physically; we just assume that when MotorForward is true, product moves eventually and sensors reflect it. In a real system, the sensors would detect product arrival; in simulation, we can treat that as external. So the logic should be: When in auto mode, if product at A (SensorA true) and ButtonA pressed, set MotorForward; when moving, if SensorB becomes true, stop MotorForward; then if product at B and ButtonB pressed, set MotorForward again; if SensorC becomes true, stop MotorForward; then if product at C and ButtonC pressed, set CompletionLight; when SensorC becomes false, turn off CompletionLight.

Edge detection: Need to detect rising edge of ButtonA, ButtonB, ButtonC to trigger actions. Also need rising edge detection of Mode to reset auto process. Also need to detect falling edge of SensorC to turn off light.

In auto mode, when moving from A to B, we need MotorForward only while product not yet at B. But also need to stop when SensorB becomes true. So we need to detect that SensorB becomes true. But in a PLC scan, when SensorB is true, we could set MotorForward false immediately; but we need to avoid toggling quickly if SensorB remains true for multiple scans. So we need to detect transition from false to true. That is rising edge detection of SensorB. Use internal variable prevSensorB.

Similarly for SensorC.

Now we also need to consider resetting auto process when mode changes to manual (or from manual to auto). The requirement says: "手动模式下正转/反转按钮互锁，两者同时按下都不动作，切到手动会清空自动流程。" So when mode becomes manual, we should clear any auto state (i.e., reset internal state to idle). So we need to detect falling edge of Mode (i.e., Mode changes from true to false). Then we reset.

Similarly, when we go from manual to auto, we need to consider the start condition: If SensorA detection and ButtonA, motor forward. But also property S8 says: "上电或从手动进入自动，A 工位有料且确认后开始向 B 输送." That is if Mode becomes true (rising edge), and SensorA and ButtonA are true (or maybe we need both ButtonA pressed). Actually S8 says: `G((Mode AND NOT prev(Mode) AND SensorA AND ButtonA) -> MotorForward)`. So we need to set MotorForward when Mode becomes true and SensorA and ButtonA are true. This could be handled by detection of rising edge of Mode.

Now property S9: "从自动开始经 A 确认、B 到位/确认、C 到位/确认的连续五拍应点亮完成灯." This is basically that after a series of states, CompletionLight should be true. This is already covered by our logic. However we need to ensure that after all steps, CompletionLight stays on as long as SensorC remains true (S10). And that it turns off when SensorC false (S5). So we can implement CompletionLight as a latched output that follows: If Mode and SensorC and ButtonC then turn on; else if not SensorC then turn off.

Now property S11: "自动方式发出新的正转命令时，必须有 A 到位并确认，或 B 到位并确认." Means whenever MotorForward is set in auto mode, either SensorA and ButtonA (i.e., moving from A) or SensorB and ButtonB (i.e., moving from B). In our logic, we will only set MotorForward when (current state = atA and ButtonA) OR (current state = atB and ButtonB). This satisfies.

Property S12: "仍在自动输送且下游 B、C 都未到位时，已运行的正转电机必须保持，不得只在启动拍发一个脉冲." Means that if we are in auto mode, previously MotorForward was true and still not at B or C (i.e., SensorB and SensorC false), we must keep MotorForward true. So we must maintain MotorForward as long as the product is in transit, not only one pulse. In our logic, we will set MotorForward = true when moving (state movingAB or movingBC). And keep it true until SensorB or SensorC detection. This will be satisfied.

Now we need to implement all these with static variables: prevMode, prevSensorA, prevSensorB, prevSensorC, prevButtonA, prevButtonB, prevButtonC maybe. Also state variable: enum (Idle, AtA, MovingAB, AtB, MovingBC, AtC). Actually we can use an integer state.

But note that the sensors may be true even when product hasn't moved yet. For example, when product is at A, SensorA true. At that moment we need to detect ButtonA pressed. So we can detect rising edge of ButtonA while SensorA true and Mode auto. Similarly for B and C.

Edge detection: Use rising edge detection: risingButtonA = ButtonA AND NOT prevButtonA. Similarly for others.

But need to consider that ButtonA may be pressed after product arrives at A, but product may remain at A for many cycles. We need to start moving only once per product. So we can have a state indicating product is at A waiting for button press. When ButtonA rising edge detected, we start moving.

Also need to handle the case where product is at B waiting for ButtonB. Use rising edge of ButtonB.

Now handle Mode switch: If Mode changes from 1 to 0 (manual), we need to clear state and set MotorForward=False, MotorReverse=False, CompletionLight=False. Also ensure no auto actions.

If Mode changes from 0 to 1 (auto), we need to check if SensorA true and ButtonA true, then start moving. Or we could wait for next scan to detect ButtonA? But property S8 says immediate start if both true at that moment. So we can set MotorForward accordingly in same scan when rising edge of Mode occurs. However, need to consider that Mode is an input; we can detect rising edge of Mode using prevMode.

Thus algorithm:

Define states: 0=Idle, 1=AtA, 2=MovingAB, 3=AtB, 4=MovingBC, 5=AtC.

When Mode=0 (manual), we ignore sensors, just handle motor forward/reverse based on buttons. Ensure mutual exclusion: MotorForward = ForwardButton AND NOT ReverseButton; MotorReverse = ReverseButton AND NOT ForwardButton. No other outputs.

When Mode=1 (auto):

- Update previous values: prevMode, prevSensorA, prevSensorB, prevSensorC, prevButtonA, prevButtonB, prevButtonC.

- Determine rising edges: risingMode = Mode AND NOT prevMode; risingButtonA = ButtonA AND NOT prevButtonA; similarly for B, C.

- Determine falling edges: fallingMode = NOT Mode AND prevMode.

- At the start of auto mode (risingMode), we need to initialize state based on sensor detection: If SensorA true, set state=AtA; else if SensorB true, maybe product already at B? But according to process, product must go through A first. However maybe after power-up product already at B. The spec may not require handling that; we can assume product always at A initially or start from whatever sensor is true. We'll handle generically: If SensorC true, set state=AtC (but then need to handle buttonC?). But simpler: We'll set state to Idle and let sensors trigger next steps. However property S8 specifically says if SensorA and ButtonA then start moving. So we can set state accordingly.

Simplify: Use a state machine that is driven by sensors and button presses. The state indicates where the product currently is and whether the motor is moving.

